# Viewing UI (cloud agents)

The user **cannot** open `localhost` on the agent VM. Never tell them to use `http://localhost:…` as the way to review UI.

## Do this instead (fast path)

1. After push, get the **Vercel Preview URL** immediately:
   - `gh pr view <n> --comments` and read the Vercel bot table, **or**
   - GitHub deployment statuses / PR checks `targetUrl` / preview link
2. Hand them that URL (append `#section` if useful, e.g. `#trust`).
3. Optionally paste 1–2 screenshots into the PR body / artifacts.

## Do not

- Spend turns on MCP auth, Firecrawl, or long tool chains just to “find a way to view”
- Say “open localhost” without also giving the preview link in the same breath
- Wait for the user to ask “how do I view this?” — surface the preview URL when UI work is pushed

## Note

Previews may require Vercel SSO for the project owner. Still give the link; screenshots are the fallback if SSO blocks them.
